    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Second son of the Comte de la Belliere, Louis Charles Fortier de la Belliere chose the army over the Church and served in colonial Canada, where in 1754 he was seduced and Embraced by a mysterious Indian shaman's agent, Night Star, after his men were slaughtered around him. He built a respected unlife in New York, fled the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat} to San Francisco and finally Los Angeles in 1912, joining Don Sebastian's primogen. When Don Sebastian savagely beat Jeremy MacNeil for defying him, Louis alone among the primogen spoke up for the anarch; when the primogen refused to act, Louis broke with them, fought alongside Jeremy and Crispus Attucks in the 1944 Revolt, and led the ill-fated expedition to Malibu. In gratitude, the anarchs let him govern West Los Angeles (Beverly Hills and the Westside) as his own barony.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>The quintessential nobleman, Louis is protective of his vassals, gracious to enemies, and the only baron who takes genuine interest in his domain's economic prosperity — the Westside thrives under his tight, paternalistic control. He respects Jeremy as a born leader and supports the Free States' \"experiment in democracy\" even though the notion of Kindred equality offends his noble sensibilities. He built the Music Center (with Jeremy) as a cultural Elysium alternative, though most anarchs showed no interest in it.</p>",
    "notes": "Haven: a magnificent, heavily guarded mansion in Beverly Hills. Keeps three formidable mistresses (Catherine, Elena, and a third) and reputedly the largest ghoul household in the Free States, all young, strong, and beautiful.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
